From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jackson Goode <54308792+jacksongoode@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:27:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] kompakt: MGLRU, backported from the Palm PVG100 kernel

MGLRU (multi-gen LRU) went into Linux 6.1. It replaces the active and
inactive lists the kernel uses to decide which memory to free, and on
low-RAM Android it means fewer reclaim stalls.

This is Kyle Anderson's 4.19 backport for the Palm PVG100, branch
pepito-24 of solarkennedy/android_kernel_xiaomi_msm8937, from 70ed3b77f6de
to 253a9ff4e4d1: the lru cleanups it depends on, Yu Zhao's MGLRU series
and Kyle's fixes, squashed into one patch.

Changed for this tree:
- context fixes in fuse, mm/Kconfig, swapfile, vmscan and the cgroup stubs,
  and the static keys placed after MediaTek's GMO block in vmscan.c
- mmap_sem in place of the mmap lock API, which 4.19 does not have
- the arch_has_hw_pte_young() stub goes in asm-generic/pgtable.h

Left out:
- 6d8e25c1c545, 7fb533c0eebe, 2c56bd8c8ea6, 5ca4fbca950d and 05eb877a1d73,
  which move the swap cache to XArray and keep shadow entries in it. This
  tree's swap cache is a radix tree, so 0056 adds the shadow entries there.
- fd88e2ecb440, a process_reclaim fix that is not part of MGLRU.

Off until CONFIG_LRU_GEN is set.
